WEBVTT

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:10.169
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, all. Friday the 27th. Everyone on? And nobody mention the football last night, please. I've suffered enough.</v>

00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:20.489
<v Grace Liu>I'm more concerned about the heating in the portakabin. It's either tropical or you can see your breath. Just having a moan, before that goes on your list.</v>

00:00:21.089 --> 00:00:25.289
<v Marcus Hale>You got tropical? Luxury. We only seem to get the other setting.</v>

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:34.060
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, yeah, I'm here. Traffic on the ring road was ridiculous. Three lanes of people looking at absolutely nothing.</v>

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, lovely. Let's start with what's finished, then the actual jobs.</v>

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:47.439
<v Callum Reid>I signed off the inspection on the outfeed conveyor on Tuesday. That's closed, not something we need to carry over.</v>

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:52.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, got that. It was still showing on the old view, that's all.</v>

00:00:53.850 --> 00:01:00.149
<v Marcus Hale>And I tested the Injection Moulding Line 3 yesterday and it's all fine now. Finished from my side.</v>

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:08.879
<v Priya Raman>Same sort of thing here: tested the line 1 TCU yesterday and it's all fine now. Nothing outstanding on that test.</v>

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.780
<v Grace Liu>Good. Actual closed items. We do occasionally have those, then.</v>

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:24.969
<v Priya Raman>Also, the shutdown on the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve is cancelled now, production need it running. So that shutdown's off, not waiting for me to do it today.</v>

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.230
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Cancelled, not deferred on today's list.</v>

00:01:31.359 --> 00:01:36.260
<v Aisha Begum>Um, two observations. Heard a slight rattle from the palletiser, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:41.079
<v Callum Reid>Right, just an observation. Not turning that into a job.</v>

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:49.530
<v Aisha Begum>And noticed the line 2 robot was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. The warmth isn't an outstanding issue.</v>

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:57.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. There's still the separate jam and sensor check on the line 2 robot, though. That's not the temperature observation.</v>

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:05.629
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the line 2 robot by Thursday. That's fairly important.</v>

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:14.340
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, talking over you—yeah, separate thing. I didn't want the warm-running comment getting muddled up with the jam.</v>

00:02:14.729 --> 00:02:18.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed. Jamie, you've got the line 2 robot, by Thursday, fairly important.</v>

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.780
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, that's mine. Clear the jam and check the sensors.</v>

00:02:24.539 --> 00:02:32.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you grease and check the bearings on the line 3 barrel today? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:45.819
<v Aisha Begum>I can't take that today, sorry. And separately, I still can't get to the fire alarm panel until production gives us a window. That's blocked; I'm not promising anything on that either.</v>

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:56.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, the fire alarm panel stays blocked. PR, can you take the line 3 barrel bearings instead of Aisha? Still today, not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:05.259
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll grease and check the bearings on the line 3 barrel today. I can take that one.</v>

00:03:06.729 --> 00:03:11.629
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. Doesn't need everyone dropping everything, just don't let it disappear into next week.</v>

00:03:12.169 --> 00:03:21.620
<v Aisha Begum>What I can commit to: I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the air dryer on the 3rd. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:28.680
<v Grace Liu>First for that slot on the 3rd, yeah? Not saying the sign-off's happening today.</v>

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:35.009
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. On the 3rd, and it needs doing first because it's holding production up.</v>

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:43.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Aisha owns the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the air dryer. On the 3rd, first because of the production hold.</v>

00:03:46.069 --> 00:03:51.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you order spare parts for the stretch wrapper at half two? Normal priority.</v>

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:57.819
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll order spare parts for the stretch wrapper at half two.</v>

00:03:58.819 --> 00:04:02.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Normal priority, so I'm not asking for a panic order.</v>

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:07.650
<v Jamie Brennan>Understood. Half two, normal priority. No dramatic phone voice required.</v>

00:04:10.069 --> 00:04:17.069
<v Sarah Okafor>While we're on purchasing, Jamie, can you chase the purchase order for the line 3 barrel next Tuesday? Low priority.</v>

00:04:19.089 --> 00:04:26.439
<v Jamie Brennan>Not that one, sorry. I haven't got the approval history in front of me, and I can't take the chase on.</v>

00:04:28.379 --> 00:04:35.730
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. PR, can I hand that to you instead—chase the purchase order for the line 3 barrel next Tuesday, low priority?</v>

00:04:36.269 --> 00:04:42.920
<v Priya Raman>Yes, I'll chase the purchase order for the line 3 barrel next Tuesday. Low priority, separate from today's bearings.</v>

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:49.639
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, could you also swap the filter on the line one HPU by Wednesday?</v>

00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:58.540
<v Priya Raman>No, sorry, I can't fit that one in as well. Bearings and the purchase order, yes; the filter, no.</v>

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:06.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Marcus, can you take over the filter swap on the line one HPU, by Wednesday?</v>

00:05:08.189 --> 00:05:14.139
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll swap the filter on the line one HPU by Wednesday. That's mine rather than PR's.</v>

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:20.600
<v Callum Reid>And I'll check the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1 by Wednesday.</v>

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:29.189
<v Grace Liu>That's Callum Reid taking the guarding check on the Injection Moulding Line 1, by Wednesday, yeah? Your audio clipped at the start.</v>

00:05:30.899 --> 00:05:35.800
<v Callum Reid>Yep, me. I'll check the guarding, by Wednesday. Teams picked a good moment there.</v>

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:45.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, can you write up the near miss at the Stretch Wrapper by the end of the week? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:52.689
<v Marcus Hale>I can't take the write-up, sorry. I wasn't there for the incident, only heard about it afterwards.</v>

00:05:54.759 --> 00:06:04.910
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Jamie Brennan, can you take that instead? Write up the near miss at the Stretch Wrapper by the end of the week. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:06:06.889 --> 00:06:16.339
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I was there. I'll write up the near miss at the Stretch Wrapper by the end of the week. Understood, it matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:22.470
<v Grace Liu>Right. That's the write-up we're agreeing, not a fresh incident response.</v>

00:06:24.579 --> 00:06:32.980
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. And we are on Friday, so by the end of the week still stands. Not urgent doesn't mean push it into next week.</v>

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:37.670
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, understood. The write-up's with me, by the end of the week.</v>

00:06:39.509 --> 00:06:44.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:06:46.129 --> 00:06:49.279
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team.</v>

00:06:49.949 --> 00:06:55.899
<v Grace Liu>Agreed on fairly important. Easy for that sort of thing to get lost among the plant jobs.</v>

00:06:57.709 --> 00:07:02.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Aisha. No date or time agreed for that here; just keeping the importance clear.</v>

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:07.110
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, mine to organise, fairly important. Got it.</v>

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:15.019
<v Callum Reid>Just so we're not leaving with two versions: the outfeed conveyor inspection is already signed off. I'm not carrying that again.</v>

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:21.889
<v Marcus Hale>And the Injection Moulding Line 3 test is done. Nothing new out of that.</v>

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:29.180
<v Priya Raman>Yep. line 1 TCU test done as well, and the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve shutdown stays cancelled.</v>

00:07:31.149 --> 00:07:36.750
<v Aisha Begum>Fire alarm panel still blocked until production gives us a window. No commitment against that today.</v>

00:07:39.129 --> 00:07:47.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. And neither the palletiser rattle nor the settled temperature on the line 2 robot is a new action. That's everything agreed, then.</v>

00:07:48.699 --> 00:07:52.199
<v Jamie Brennan>Good. This meeting moved quicker than the ring road, anyway.</v>

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:58.709
<v Grace Liu>Low bar. I'm ending the call before the portakabin switches back to Arctic.</v>

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, cheers, everyone.</v>
